  "body": "Asked by mkinney (2026-11-18): \"Can you create a p3 doc issue for that tools export. If you can import tools, add that too. I might want to import tools for future tests on hub.\"\n\n## What a Tormach user has today\n\nPathPilot can export and import its whole tool table as a `.csv` file (Tormach 770MX operator manual UM10587, section 7.6.4 \"Import and Export the Tool Table\"): **Offsets tab -> Export -> type a name -> save to a USB drive**; **Import** on the same tab loads a `.csv` back. PathPilot Hub has the same Offsets tab.\n\nCamCraft today:\n- imports and exports tool libraries only as `.camtools` (`import_tool_library`, `export_tool_library`, #355, #899);\n- writes a setup's tool list as a generic CSV for a spreadsheet (`tool_list_export.rs`, #389) - not PathPilot's column layout;\n- has no docs page that tells a Tormach user how to get his machine's tools into CamCraft.\n\nSo a user re-types every tool (number, diameter, length, description) to make posted programs match the machine.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. **Docs** (site guide, Tormach section): how to export the PathPilot tool table (the steps above), how to bring it into CamCraft, and how the tool numbers map to `T<n>` in the posted program. Same page: the reverse, for PathPilot Hub tests.\n2. **Import:** read a PathPilot tool-table `.csv` into the document's tools (or a `.camtools` library): tool number, diameter, length/offset, type and description where the file has them; the user completes what PathPilot does not store (flutes, flute length, holder). One undo step; an MCP tool (or a format option on `import_tool_library`); refuse by name a row it cannot read.\n3. **Export (for Hub and the real machine):** write the document's tools as a PathPilot tool-table `.csv` that PathPilot's Import reads, so a Hub test or a real job starts with the same tool numbers and diameters as the posted program.\n\n## Open point\n\nThe exact PathPilot CSV columns are not in the manual. mkinney will export his 770MX tool table; that file is the sample to build and pin the parser against (tests with a recorded `.csv`, no machine needed).\n\nDone means: a docs page with the export/import steps; an import that reads the sample file into tools with the right numbers and diameters, pinned by a test; an export that PathPilot Hub imports (checked once in Hub).\n",
